  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-or300.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Or 309.06 Cargo Truck Use by Industrial Enterprises or the Military",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Or 309.06 Cargo Truck Use by Industrial Enterprises or the Military.\n\n(a) The use of cargo trucks by an industrial enterprise or the military shall be authorized, subject to the conditions noted in (b), below, if such use is required to:\n\n(1) Deliver fuel to the fuel tanks of stationary equipment, off-road earthmoving equipment, military tactical vehicles, parked aircraft, or parked refrigeration trailers, provided the cargo truck or trailer shall not be used for on-site storage of oil except as allowed by (2), below; or\n\n(2) To hold oil removed from an AST system during maintenance activities, provided the cargo truck or trailer shall not be used for distribution for end use of the oil.\n\n(b) Except as allowed by (c), below, or as approved by the state fire marshal, cargo trucks and trailers shall not be used to deliver fuel to on-road motor vehicles.\n\n(c) The use of cargo trucks by military personnel to support military vehicles in convoy shall be allowed provided there is an applicable oil spill and response plan, prepared pursuant to 49 CFR 130.31, which requires:\n\n(1) The use of portable flexible containment areas; and\n\n(2) Proper containment and disposal of any spilled oil.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Or 300) #10487, eff 2-7-14; ss by #14094, eff 10-4-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-or300.html"
